### What Sun shows without words, in pa3ds's own words, a beat at a time, said under [pa3ds.ui]
### descriptions. When each is said is `../scenes.toml`'s, every language's; a beat is found here
### by its id there (ADR-0040). A name the game shows is never written here.

# The chase after Kukui's call, demo 6, unskippable. Before it the camera leaves the monitor for
# the desk; the game says "Three months later..." itself at 71 s, and the field takes over at about
# 89 s with the arrival, which plays without the player until Mom speaks at about 114 s. The
# arrival's beats wait for the field, Route 1's zone 0x0, which came 91 s after the demo started in
# movie1_opening.ctm (2026-10-13).
chase-1 = After the call, the camera turned to your desk: a travel magazine open on pictures of tropical islands, and a plane ticket.
chase-2 = Somewhere else, a girl in a white sun hat and white dress runs through a gleaming white building, a big bag over her shoulder.
chase-3 = She stops at a railing and looks back, holding the bag close.
chase-4 = She runs on into a glass-roofed garden, along a white bridge through the trees.
chase-5 = Men in white uniforms and caps are after her. One blocks the bridge ahead.
chase-6 = They close in, one of them grinning. She stops, clutching the bag.
chase-7 = A burst of blue light flares around her.
chase-8 = A glowing ball of light rises through the glass roof into the sky.
chase-9 = The game's title logo appears.
chase-10 = From high above: a green island ringed by reefs, with a town by the harbour and an old volcano crater.
chase-11 = On the ground: a seaside lawn with palm trees and a low fence. A boy in a white shirt walks across the grass.
chase-12 = A grey wooden house on stilts, with a porch, steps and a mailbox. A small Pokémon trots by.
